  (@custom "contractspecv0" (after data) "\00\00\00\00\00\00\04\00Pay this contract's storage rent without doing anything else.\0a\0aTakes no auth and names no caller. Topping up rent cannot harm\0aanyone -- the caller spends their own fee to extend an entry\0anobody else is charged for -- and gating it behind a privileged\0akey would mean a dormant contract could only be rescued by\0awhoever still held that key.\0a\0aThe internal bumps are lazy on purpose: they act only once an\0aentry is within [`TTL_THRESHOLD`] of archival, so an ordinary\0acaller almost never pays rent. The cost of that is a lottery.\0aWhen the threshold is finally crossed the whole top-up lands on\0awhichever transaction is next through the door, and because the\0ainstance bump carries the contract's code entry with it, that is\0athe largest single entry here. Measured on the roster, whose wasm\0ais half the size of this one: 21.79 XLM for the transaction that\0apaid, 0.095 XLM for the next one.\0a\0aThis is the other half of that design. A keeper calling `bump`\0atops the entries back up whatever their remaining life, so the\0acost tracks h\00\00\00\04bump\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\04\00\00\00\00\00\00\04\00Transfer ownership of a spend-mode token: move the owner pointer to\0a`new_owner_commitment`, burning the current owner's claim.\0a\0a`caller.require_auth()` covers the tx fee only \e2\80\94 **ownership is proven by\0athe Ed25519 owner-key signature, not the tx source**, so any funded\0aaccount may relay a spend. The current owner signs\0a`SHA-256(SPEND_AUTH || contract_xdr || slot_id (u32 BE) ||\0aephemeral_key || current_commitment || new_commitment ||\0aspend_nonce (u32 BE))` \e2\80\94 the format in\0a`docs/architecture/spend-mode.md`, which this must agree with letter\0afor letter; a signer that signs the digest blind relies on it.\0a\0aEach field earns its place. Both commitments stop the spend being\0areplayed against a moved state and stop an observer swapping the\0asuccessor; the nonce makes the authorisation good for exactly one\0atransfer, which the commitments alone do not, because a note that\0areturns to a commitment it held before reproduces the old digest;\0athe contract address stops a signature crossing deployments; the\0aslot is the recor\00\00\00\05spend\00\00\00\00\00\00\05\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\06caller\00\00\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\07slot_id\00\00\00\00\04\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\14current_owner_pubkey\00\00\03\ee\00\00\00 \00\00\00\00\00\00\00\14new_owner_commitment\00\00\03\ee\00\00\00 \00\00\00\00\00\00\00\09signature\00\00\00\00\00\03\ee\00\00\00@\00\00\00\01\00\00\03\e9\00\00\03\ed\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\03\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\06roster\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\00\00\00\00tDissolve the caller's registered pair. Either member may; the\0apartner's record goes too. Returns the former partner.\00\00\00\06unpair\00\00\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\06caller\00\00\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\01\00\00\03\e9\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\03\00\00\00\00\00\00\00)The pair `node` is registered in, if any.\00\00\00\00\00\00\07pair_of\00\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\04node\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\01\00\00\03\e8\00\00\07\d0\00\00\00\0eRegisteredPair\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00SA print slot, assembled from its core and its draw. `lapsed` says\0athe draw is gone.\00\00\00\00\08get_slot\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\07slot_id\00\00\00\00\04\00\00\00\01\00\00\03\e8\00\00\07\d0\00\00\00\09PrintSlot\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\08node_fee\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\04\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\09get_token\00\00\00\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\07slot_id\00\00\00\00\04\00\00\00\01\00\00\03\e8\00\00\07\d0\00\00\00\0bTokenRecord\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\09max_pairs\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\04\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\09min_pairs\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\04\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\09pay_token\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\