er posts it has nothing to\0achoose, and withholding it only delays the print.\0a\0a`signature` is the round's G1 signature, uncompressed. A point off\0athe curve or outside the subgroup traps in the host before any\0apairing; a valid point that is not this round's signature is\0a`BadBeacon`.\00\00\00\00\0aseed_print\00\00\00\00\00\02\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\07slot_id\00\00\00\00\04\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\09signature\00\00\00\00\00\03\ee\00\00\00`\00\00\00\01\00\00\03\e9\00\00\03\ee\00\00\00 \00\00\00\03\00\00\00\00\00\00\01YWhether this slot has been redeemed.\0a\0aInformational, and it can lapse: the marker is not bumped, so\0aonce it archives this answers `false` about a note that was\0aredeemed. Nothing safety-critical rests on it. A holder asking\0awhether a note can still be cashed is answered by `get_token`,\0awhich returns nothing for a redeemed note and fails closed.\00\00\00\00\00\00\0bis_redeemed\00\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\07slot_id\00\00\00\00\04\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\00\00\00\00?The ledger a slot was redeemed on, if the marker is still live.\00\00\00\00\0bredeemed_at\00\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\07slot_id\00\00\00\00\04\00\00\00\01\00\00\03\e8\00\00\00\04\00\00\00\00\00\00\00;Accrued, unclaimed node-fee balance for `node` (0 if none).\00\00\00\00\0caccrued_fees\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\04node\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0ccancel_print\00\00\00\02\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\06caller\00\00\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\07slot_id\00\00\00\00\04\00\00\00\01\00\00\03\e9\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\03\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0cconfirm_link\00\00\00\04\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\06caller\00\00\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\07slot_id\00\00\00\00\04\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0alink_index\00\00\00\00\00\04\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\12partial_public_key\00\00\00\00\03\ee\00\00\00 \00\00\00\01\00\00\03\e9\00\00\00\04\00\00\00\03\00\00\00\00\00\00\00mAll monetary parameters are immutable after construction.\0aNo admin keys, no upgrade path, no fund withdrawal.\00\00\00\00\00\00\0d__constructor\00\00\00\00\00\00\07\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\08node_fee\00\00\00\04\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\09min_pairs\00\00\00\00\00\00\04\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\09max_pairs\00\00\00\00\00\00\04\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\09pay_token\00\00\00\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\06roster\00\00\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\11max_print_ledgers\00\00\00\00\00\00\04\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\09selection\00\00\00\00\00\07\d0\00\00\00\0fSelectionConfig\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\01\f7Path A (pure bearer): redeem by proving knowledge of the composed\0aephemeral secret. The holder signs\0a`SHA-256(domain_tag || contract_xdr || slot_id (u32 BE) ||\0aephemeral_key || recipient_xdr)`.\0a\0aThe recipient is in the digest because `require_auth()` does **not**\0abind it \e2\80\94 that binds whoever submits the transaction, while the\0asignature would otherwise be a standalone credential anyone could\0areuse. **Rejects spend-mode tokens** \e2\80\94 those must use\0a[`redeem_by_key_owned`](Self::redeem_by_key_owned).\00\00\00\00\0dredeem_by_key\00\00\00\00\00\00\05\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\06holder\00\00\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\09recipient\00\00\00\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\07slot_id\00\00\00\00\04\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\09signature\00\00\00\00\00\03\ee\00\00\00@\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0fclaim_signature\00\00\00\03\ee\00\00\00@\00\00\00\01\00\00\03\e9\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\03\00\00\00\00\00\00\01KRegister `(node_a, node_b)` as a pair, so it may claim positions on\0aprints requested from the next ledger on.\0a\0aBoth sign; both must be selectable on the roster and old enough\0a(`min_node_age`); and each address is in at most one registered\0apair, so a set of addresses cannot be re-combined per draw. Returns\0athe registration ledger.\00\00\00\00\0dregister_pair\00\00\00\00\00\00\02\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\06node_a\00\00\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\06node_b\00\00\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\01\00\00\03\e9\00\00\00\04\00\00\00\03\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\9eReserve a slot and escrow the deposit, naming only the depositor's\0aown two end pairs. The interior is chosen by the draw:\0a`seed_print`, then `claim_position`.\00\00\00\00\00\0drequest_print\00\00\00\00\00\00\06\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\06caller\00\00\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\08event_id\00\00\03\ee\00\00\00 \00\00\00\00\00\00\00\06amount\00\00\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0btotal_pairs\00\00\00\00\04\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0afirst_pair\00\00\00\00\07\d0\00\00\00\09PairEntry\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\09last_pair\00\00\00\00\00\07\d0\00\00\00\09PairEntry\00\00\00\00\00\00\01\00\00\03\e9\00\00\00\04\00\00\00\03\00\00\00\00\00\00\03QSeed a slot the beacon never seeded, once its round has been due for\0a`fallback_delay` seconds. Anyone may call it, and the seed is fixed\0aby the slot, so the caller has nothing to choose.\0a\0a**This keeps issuance alive if drand stops**, for minutes or for\0agood; without it every print would wait out its window and be\0arefunded. The price is that the fallback seed is computable from\0athe request onward: while the beacon is down, a depositor can pick\0athe moment they request, and so their draw. That buys fee capture,\0athe same as steering always did (`docs/architecture/\0anode-selection.md`), never another holder's funds. While the beacon\0ais up, round `R` is posted long before the fallback opens, so the\0afallback is never used.\0a\0aEverything after the seed is unchanged: claims, the window, and the\0aforfeit, which treats a fallback-seeded slot as seeded.\00\00\00\00\00\00\0dseed_fallback\00\00\00\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\07slot_id\00\00\00\00\04\00\00\00\01\00\00\03\e9\00\00\03\ee\00\00\00 \00\00\00\03\00\00\00\00\00\00\02\06Replace the selected pair at the next position with the best\0arunner-up, because it did not confirm within `serve_timeout`.\0a\0a**The depositor pays one pair's fee, `2 * node_fee`, burned.** The\0acontract cannot tell a dead node from a depositor who never sent the\0aextend request, so skipping has to cost something, or it would be a\0afree way to steer positions toward one's own runners-up. It is\0acharged from the depositor rather than the escrow, so the escrow\0astays equal to the note's face.\0a\0aReturns the position skipped.\00\00\00\00\00\0dskip_position\00\00\00\00\00\00\02\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\06caller\00\00\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\07slot_id\00\00\00\00\04\00\00\00\01\00\00\03\e9\00\00\00\04\00\00\00\03\00\00\00\00\00\00\01\9eClaim an interior position for the pair `(node_a, node_b)`.\0a\0aBoth members sign: otherwise anyone could enter an honest pair into\0aa print it never agreed to serve. The score is\0acomputed here from the seed and the pair, so it cannot be chosen,\0aand a later claim with a lower score displaces a higher one until\0aselection closes -- being first earns nothing.\0a\0aReturns the claim's rank, 0 being the lowest score so far.\00\00\00\00\00\0eclaim_position\00\00\00\00\00\03\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\07slot_id\00\00\00\00\04\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\06node_a\00\00\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\06node_b\00\00\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\01\00\00\03\e9\00\00\00\04\00\00\00\03\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0eregister_token\00\00\00\00\00\07\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\06caller\00\00\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\07slot_id\00\00\00\00\04\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0dephemeral_key\00\00\00\00\00\03\ee\00\00\00 \00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0achain_hash\00\00\00\00\03\ee\00\00\00 \00\00\00\00\00\00\00\04mode\00\00\07\d0\00\00\00\09TokenMode\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\18initial_owner_commitment\00\00\03\ee\00\00\00 \00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0cclaim_pubkey\00\00\03\ee\00\00\00 \00\00\00\01\00\00\03\e9\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\03\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0fget_token_state\00\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\07slot_id\00\00\00\00\04\00\00\00\01\00\00\03\e8\00\00\07\d0\00\00\00\0aTokenState\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0fis_slot_expired\00\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\07slot_id\00\00\00\00\04\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\00\00\00\01\0ePath B (pure bearer): redeem by submitting the full signature chain.\0aOn-chain verification of dual Ed25519 signatures + hash chain. Node fees\0aaccrue to participants. **Rejects spend-mode tokens** \e2\80\94 those must use\0a[`redeem_by_chain_owned`](Self::redeem_by_chain_owned).\00\00\00\00\00\0fredeem_by_chain\00\00\00\00\05\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\06holder\00\00\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\09recipient\00\00\00\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\07slot_id\00\00\00\00\04\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0achain_data\00\00\00\00\00\0e\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0fclaim_signature\00\00\00\03\ee\00\00\00@\00\00\00\01\00\00\03\e9\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\03\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\11max_print_ledgers\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\04\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\12clear_expired_slot\00\00\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\07slot_id\00\00\00\00\04\00\00\00\01\00\00\03\e9\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\03\00\00\00\00\00\00\01\16Path A for spend-mode tokens: as [`redeem_by_key`](Self::redeem_by_key),\0aplus the current owner opens the live `owner_commitment` and signs\0a`SHA-256(SPEND_REDEEM || contract_xdr || slot_id (u32 BE) ||\0aephemeral_key || owner_commitment || spend_nonce (u32 BE) ||\0arecipient_xdr)`.\00\00\00\00\00\13redeem_by_key_owned\00\00\00\00\06\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\06holder\00\00\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\09recipient\00\00\00\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\07slot_id\00\00\00\00\04\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\09signature\00\00\00\00\00\03\ee\00\00\00@\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0cowner_pubkey\00\00\03\ee\00\00\00 \00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0fowner_signature\00\00\00\03\ee\00\00\00@\00\00\00\01\00\00\03\e9\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\03\00\00\00\00\00\00\01\1aPath B for spend-mode tokens: as [`redeem_by_chain`](Self::redeem_by_chain),\0aplus the current owner opens the live `owner_commitment` and signs\0a`SHA-256(SPEND_REDEEM || contract_xdr || slot_id (u32 BE) ||\0aephemeral_key || owner_commitment || spend_nonce (u32 BE) ||\0arecipient_xdr)`.\00\00\00\00\00\15redeem_by_chain_owned\00\00\00\00\00\00\06\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\06holder\00\00\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\09recipient\00\00\00\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\07slot_id\00\00\00\00\04\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0achain_data\00\00\00\00\00\0e\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0cowner_pubkey\00\00\03\ee\00\00\00 \00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0fowner_signature\00\00\00\03\ee\00\00\00@\00\00\00\01\00\00\03\e9\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\03\00\00\00\01\00\00\00-A pair's claim on a print, ranked by `score`.\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\05Claim\00\00\00\00\00\00\04\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\04pair\00\00\07\d0\00\00\00\09PairEntry\00\00\00\00\00\00}`sha256(seed || lower || higher)` over the pair's two addresses'\0aXDR, ordered bytewise. Computed by the mint, never supplied.\00\00\00\00\00\00\05score\00\00\00\00\00\03\ee\00\00\00 \00\00\003Each member's terms, from the roster at claim time.\00\00\00\00\0bvolunteer_a\00\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0bvolunteer_b\00\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\04\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\05Error\00\00\00\00\00\00)\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\10InvalidPairCount\00\00\00\14\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0fNodeNotOnRoster\00\00\00\00\15\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0cSlotNotFound\00\00\00\16\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0fSlotNotPrinting\00\00\00\00\17\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0bSlotExpired\00\00\00\00\18\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0fNotAssignedPair\00\00\00\00\19\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0eLinkOutOfOrder\00\00\00\00\00\1a\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\14PrintAlreadyComplete\00\00\00\1b\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0cNotDepositor\00\00\00\1c\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\10PrintNotComplete\00\00\00\1d\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0eSlotNotExpired\00\00\00\00\00\1e\00\00\01nA pair whose two nodes are the same address, or a node that\0aappears in more than one pair of the same print.\0a\0aA \22pair\22 of one node is not a pair: the two-party construction is\0awhat makes a shard take two parties to produce, and one operator\0aholding both halves of a link -- or every link -- collapses that\0ato a single point of trust while still looking like a chain.\00\00\00\00\00\10NodesNotDistinct\00\00\00\1f\00\00\002This `event_id` has been used by an earlier print.\00\00\00\00\00\0cEventIdInUse\00\00\00 \00\00\000The slot's beacon round has not been posted yet.\00\00\00\09NotSeeded\00\00\00\00\00\00!\00\00\001`seed_print` on a slot that already has its seed.\00\00\00\00\00\00\0dAlreadySeeded\00\00\00\00\00\00\22\00\00\00DThe signature does not verify as the beacon's for this slot's round.\00\00\00\09BadBeacon\00\00\00\00\00\00#\00\00\00ZNo more claims: selection has closed, or the window has passed\0awith every position filled.\00\00\00\00\00\0cClaimsClosed\00\00\00$\00\00\00AThe claim list is full and this score is not lower than its last.\00\00\00\00\00\00\13ClaimNotCompetitive\00\00\00\00%\00\00\00iInterior links wait for selection: the window has not passed, or\0afewer pairs than positions have claimed.\00\00\00\00\00\00\11SelectionNotReady\00\00\00\00\00\00&\00\00\00\1eEvery runner-up has been used.\00\00\00\00\00\08NoBackup\00\00\00'\00\00\00R`seed_fallback` before the slot's round has been due for\0a`fallback_delay` seconds.\00\00\00\00\00\10FallbackNotReady\00\00\00<\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0dTokenNotFound\00\00\00\00\00\00(\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0eTokenNotActive\00\00\00\00\00)\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0fAlreadyRedeemed\00\00\00\00*\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\10InvalidSignature\00\00\00+\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\17ChainVerificationFailed\00\00\00\00,\00\00\02\edA record already exists for this slot.\0a\0a**Unreachable in practice, and kept deliberately.** Registration\0amust never write over an existing entry: `ephemeral_key` is the\0asum of the partial public keys `confirm_link` publishes, so anyone\0awatching the ledger can compute one.\0a\0aRecords are keyed by **slot**, and `register_token` requires a\0a`Printing` slot and deletes it, so a second registration is\0arefused as `SlotNotFound` before this check runs. The check stays because it\0aguards the nullifier directly instead of relying on an invariant\0aabout a different key.\0a\0aNote what is *not* prevented: a redeemed `ephemeral_key` can be\0aregistered again under a **new slot**. That is a separate record\0awith its own escrow, and it takes nothing from the first.\00\00\00\00\00\00\0bTokenExists\00\00\00\001\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0eNothingToClaim\00\00\00\00\00-\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0cNotSpendMode\00\00\00.\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\16SpendModeRequiresOwner\00\00\00\00\00/\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\17OwnerCommitmentMismatch\00\00\00\000\00\00\00\e1A payout or a participant slot named this contract.\0a\0aThe escrow would leave the books and arrive back in the same\0abalance with nothing recording that it is owed to anyone -- not\0astolen, but unreachable, and the note consumed.\00\00\00\00\00\00\0cPayoutToSelf\00\00\002\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0dInvalidAmount\00\00\00\00\00\003\00\00\01\0dThe constructor was given parameters no print could ever satisfy.\0a\0aA mint is immutable, so a deployment that cannot mint is permanent:\0athe only remedy is to deploy again and tell everyone the old address\0ais dead. Rejecting at construction is the one chance to catch it.\00\00\00\00\00\00\0dInvalidConfig\00\00\00\00\00\004\00\00\00BThe pair at this position has not yet had `serve_timeout` ledgers.\00\00\00\00\00\16ServeTimeoutNotReached\00\00\00\00\005\00\00\00/Only the next interior position can be skipped.\00\00\00\00\0cNotSkippable\00\00\006\00\00\00LA member of the pair joined the roster less than `min_node_age`\0aledgers ago.\00\00\00\0aNodeTooNew\00\00\00\00\007\00\00\00EOne of the addresses is already in a registered pair; `unpair` first.\00\00\00\00\00\00\0dAlreadyPaired\00\00\00\00\00\008\00\00\00$The caller is in no registered pair.\00\00\00\09NotPaired\00\00\00\00\00\009\00\00\00BThe claim is not a pair registered before this slot was requested.\00\00\00\00\00\11PairNotRegistered\00\00\00\00\00\00:\00\00\00\e3The slot's draw (`DataKey::Draw`) has lapsed while the slot is\0astill inside its window. Reachable only on a mint whose window is\0alonger than the network's `max_entry_ttl`, after that long with no\0awrite. Cancel still settles it.\00\00\00\00\0aDrawLapsed\00\00\00\00\00;\00\00\00\02\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\07DataKey\00\00\00\00\09\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\06Config\00\00\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\04Slot\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\04\00\00\00\01\00\00\02\faA registered note, keyed by the **slot** that produced it.\0a\0aNot keyed by `ephemeral_key`: that is a caller-named value that is\0apublic before its owner registers it (`confirm_link` publishes the\0apartial keys, and `ek` is their sum). With registration refusing to\0aoverwrite, an `ek` key would make it \22first to name the key wins\22:\0aanyone with a parked completed slot could claim a victim's key the\0amoment it became computable, and the victim's print could never be\0aregistered at all.\0a\0aA slot id is issued by the contract, not chosen by a caller, so\0atwo prints cannot collide. Two slots naming the same `ek`\0aare simply two records: each has its own escrow, chain hash and\0aclaim key, and a squatter only puts their own deposit within\0areach of whoever holds that key.\00\00\00\00\00\05Token\00\00\00\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\04\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0aNextSlotId\00\00\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\86Claimable node-fee balance for a node address (churn-tolerant earnings).\0aCredited at redemption (both paths), drained by `claim_fees`.\00\00\00\00\00\07Accrued\00\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\01\00\00\01\84Marks an `event_id` as spent, so no second print can claim it.\0a\0aThe chain hash already binds a chain to its token, so this is not the thing standing between a forged chain and an\0aescrow -- but an `event_id` is how every off-chain party names a\0aprint, and two prints answering to one name is a reconciliation\0aproblem nobody can fix after the fact. Written once per print and\0anever removed.\00\00\00\0bEventIdUsed\00\00\00\00\01\00\00\03\ee\00\00\00 \00\00\00\01\00\00\03\c9A redeemed slot, and the ledger it was redeemed on.\0a\0aThis replaces the whole `TokenRecord` once a note is paid out.\0aThe record is not needed as the nullifier: a second redemption is refused because\0athe record it needs is *absent*, not because it is present and\0asays `Redeemed`. Slot ids come from `NextSlotId` and are never\0areused, so a deleted slot can never be resurrected -- the\0acounter is the nullifier, and the ~450-byte record would only pay\0arent to restate what the counter already guarantees.\0a\0aWhat the marker buys back is the difference between \22redeemed\22\0aand \22never existed\22, which absence alone cannot express. It is\0adeliberately *not* bumped: on-chain reads restore it\0aautomatically when a redemption attempt names it, so refusing a\0adouble-redeem stays correct forever, while the off-ledger\0aconvenience of `is_redeemed` lapses when it archives. Safety\0adoes not rest on it -- a holder asking \22can I redeem this?\22 is\0aanswered by `get_token` returning nothing.\00\00\00\00\00\00\08Redeemed\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\04\00\00\00\01\00\00\017The pair an address is registered in, and when (`register_pair`).\0a\0aPairs are fixed before a draw so an operator cannot choose which of\0aits addresses to combine after the seed is public: a score is a hash\0aof the combination, so free re-pairing let `n` staked addresses try\0a`n(n-1)/2` pairings against every seed.\00\00\00\00\06PairOf\00\00\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\01\00\00\02 The growing half of a print slot, in **temporary** storage\0a(`docs/architecture/node-selection.md`, \22Where a slot lives\22): its\0apairs, seed, claims, partial keys and confirmers. `Slot(id)` keeps the escrow and every\0afixed-size fact, and never changes size after `request_print`.\0a\0aRent is charged on an entry's growth for its whole remaining life,\0aand a persistent entry lives at least 120 days on mainnet whatever\0athe contract asks. Kept on the slot, a claim would cost a node\0a~0.045 XLM; here it rents at the temporary rate for the print window.\00\00\00\04Draw\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\04\00\00\00\01\00\00\01\14What `DataKey::Slot` stores: the escrow and every fixed-size fact of a\0aprint. Written at `request_print` and rewritten at the **same size**\0aafter, so its 120-day mainnet rent is paid once, by the depositor.\0aAssembled with [`SlotDraw`] into the\0a[`PrintSlot`] every reader sees.\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\08SlotCore\00\00\00\10\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\06amount\00\00\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0cbeacon_round\00\00\00\06\00\00\00<0 until seeded, so it also says whether the slot was seeded.\00\00\00\0eclaim_deadline\00\00\00\00\00\04\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\06closed\00\00\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0fcompleted_links\00\00\00\00\04\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0acreated_at\00\00\00\00\00\04\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\09depositor\00\00\00\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\08event_id\00\00\03\ee\00\00\00 \00\00\00\00\00\00\00\06filled\00\00\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0afirst_pair\00\00\00\00\07\d0\00\00\00\09PairEntry\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\09last_pair\00\00\00\00\00\07\d0\00\00\00\09PairEntry\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0dlast_progress\00\00\00\00\00\00\04\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\07slot_id\00\00\00\00\04\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\05state\00\00\00\00\00\07\d0\00\00\00\0aTokenState\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0btotal_pairs\00\00\00\00\04\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0avolunteers\00\00\00\00\00\04\00\00\00\01\00\00\00nWhat `DataKey::Draw` stores, in temporary storage: the parts of a\0aprint that grow as it is selected and built.\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\08SlotDraw\00\00\00\05\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\06claims\00\00\00\00\03\ea\00\00\07\d0\00\00\00\05Claim\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0aconfirmers\00\00\00\00\03\ea\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\05pairs\00\00\00\00\00\03\ea\00\00\07\d0\00\00\00\09PairEntry\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0cpartial_keys\00\00\03\ea\00\00\03\ee\00\00\00 \00\00\00\00\00\00\00\04seed\00\00\03\e8\00\00\03\ee\00\00\00 \00\00\00\01\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\09PairEntry\00\00\00\00\00\00\02\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\06node_a\00\00\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\06node_b\00\00\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\01\00\00\00>A pair registered (`registered`) or dissolved (`!registered`).\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\09PairEvent\00\00\00\00\00\00\03\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\06node_a\00\00\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\06node_b\00\00\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0aregistered\00\00\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\09PrintSlot\00\00\00\00\00\00\14\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\06amount\00\00\00\00\00\0b\00\00\008The beacon round that seeds this slot, fixed at request.\00\00\00\0cbeacon_round\00\00\00\06\00\00\004The last ledger of the claim window; 0 until seeded.\00\00\00\0eclaim_deadline\00\00\00\00\00\04\00\00\00\91Before closing: every competitive claim, lowest score first,\0acapped at `2k`. After: the runners-up only, in the order they\0areplace skipped pairs.\00\00\00\00\00\00\06claims\00\00\00\00\03\ea\00\00\07\d0\00\00\00\05Claim\00\00\00\00\00\00?Whether the interior positions are fixed (`pairs` is complete).\00\00\00\00\06closed\00\00\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0fcompleted_links\00\00\00\00\04\00\00\01]Who confirmed each link, in link order.\0a\0a`confirm_link` accepts either member of the assigned pair, and a\0ashard is derivable by one of them alone -- so \22this pair worked\22\0ais not something the chain can see. Only \22this address\0aconfirmed\22 is. Abandoned-slot settlement pays the confirmer and\0anobody else, because that is the whole of what is provable.\00\00\00\00\00\00\0aconfirmers\00\00\00\00\03\ea\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0acreated_at\00\00\00\00\00\04\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\09depositor\00\00\00\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\08event_id\00\00\03\ee\00\00\00 \00\00\00\b4Whether the claim list ever held `k` claims. It never shrinks below\0a`k` before closing, so this is the one fact about the claims the\0aforfeit needs, kept where it outlives the draw.\00\00\00\06filled\00\00\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\e2The draw (`DataKey::Draw`) has lapsed: `pairs` holds only the end\0apairs and `seed`, `claims`, `partial_keys` and `confirmers` are\0aempty because they are gone, not because nothing happened. Only\0asettlement works on such a slot.\00\00\00\00\00\06lapsed\00\00\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\aeThe ledger the current position became current: when selection\0aclosed, or when the previous link was confirmed or skipped. A skip\0ais allowed `serve_timeout` ledgers after it.\00\00\00\00\00\0dlast_progress\00\00\00\00\00\00\04\00\00\01*The pairs in chain order, once selection closes.\0a\0aUntil then it holds only the depositor's two end pairs,\0a`[first, last]`: the interior positions are nobody's to name\0auntil the draw is in. Closing\0ainserts the `k` winning claims between them, and a skip replaces\0aone interior entry with a runner-up.\00\00\00\00\00\05pairs\00\00\00\00\00\03\ea\00\00\07\d0\00\00\00\09PairEntry\00\00\00\00\00\02TEach confirmed link's partial public key, in link order.\0a\0a**Published, not checked.** Nothing on-chain reads these: Soroban\0aexposes no Curve25519 point addition, so the contract cannot sum\0athem and compare against the `ephemeral_key` a depositor supplies\0ato `register_token`. They are here so that anyone watching the\0aledger can do that sum themselves and confirm the key a note\0aclaims is the key its construction produced.\0a\0aThey are therefore evidence for observers, not a constraint on\0athe depositor. Their presence in the slot is not a binding, and\0aan on-chain reader must not treat it as one.\00\00\00\0cpartial_keys\00\00\03\ea\00\00\03\ee\00\00\00 \00\00\009Set by `seed_print` from that round's verified signature.\00\00\00\00\00\00\04seed\00\00\03\e8\00\00\03\ee\00\00\00 \00\00\00\00\00\00\00\07slot_id\00\00\00\00\04\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\05state\00\00\00\00\00\07\d0\00\00\00\0aTokenState\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0btotal_pairs\00\00\00\00\04\00\00\02EWhich participants volunteer: bit `2i` is pair `i`'s `node_a`,\0abit `2i + 1` its `node_b`, the same order as\0a`TokenRecord::participants`. A volunteer's fees are burned, not\0acredited.\0a\0aTaken from the roster's `node_terms` once, when the pair claims\0a(recorded in its [`Claim`]), and set here when selection closes or\0aa skip brings in a runner-up. A node is paid on the terms it had\0awhen it claimed, and nothing after the print has to consult the\0aroster. End pairs are never set: they are the depositor's and draw\0ano fee.\0a`MAX_REDEEMABLE_PAIRS = 12` is 24 participants, inside a `u32`.\00\00\00\00\00\00\0avolunteers\00\00\00\00\00\04\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\8cThe depositor skipped a selected pair that did not serve, and a\0arunner-up took its place. `fee` is what the depositor paid to do it,\0aburned.\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\09SkipEvent\00\00\00\00\00\00\05\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\03fee\00\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\08position\00\00\00\04\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0breplacement\00\00\00\07\d0\00\00\00\09PairEntry\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\07skipped\00\00\00\07\d0\00\00\00\09PairEntry\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\07slot_id\00\00\00\00\04\00\00\00\03\00\00\01\8ePer-token spend mode, fixed at `register_token`. See\0a`docs/architecture/spend-mode.md`.\0a\0a- `PureBearer` \e2\80\94 whoever holds the bytes can redeem;\0a`owner_commitment` is unused.\0a- `Spend` \e2\80\94 an on-ledger owner pointer (`owner_commitment`) that the current\0aowner moves via `spend` (burning their claim) and that redemption requires\0aopening (the owner-checked redeem paths). Prevents payer double-spend.\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\09TokenMode\00\00\00\00\00\00\02\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0aPureBearer\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\05Spend\00\00\00\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\01\00\00\00>A claim was accepted at `rank` (0 is the lowest score so far).\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0aClaimEvent\00\00\00\00\00\04\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\04pair\00\00\07\d0\00\00\00\09PairEntry\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\04rank\00\00\00\04\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\05score\00\00\00\00\00\03\ee\00\00\00 \00\00\00\00\00\00\00\07slot_id\00\00\00\00\04\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0aMintConfig\00\00\00\00\00\09\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\09max_pairs\00\00\00\00\00\00\04\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\11max_print_ledgers\00\00\00\00\00\00\04\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\09min_pairs\00\00\00\00\00\00\04\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\08node_fee\00\00\00\04\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\09pay_token\00\00\00\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\06roster\00\00\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\1eHow interior pairs are chosen.\00\00\00\00\00\09selection\00\00\00\00\00\07\d0\00\00\00\0fSelectionConfig\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0cstart_ledger\00\00\00\04\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\06symbol\00\00\00\00\00\11\00\00\00\01\00\00\01\b6The roster's `Node` record, as `get_node` returns it, read here only\0afor `joined_at` (`min_node_age`).\0a\0aA `contracttype` struct crosses contracts as a map keyed by field\0aname, so this must name the same fields with the same types as\0a`kenter-roster`'s `Node`. The roster is immutable, so it cannot drift\0aunder a deployed mint; `test::the_mock_roster_node_matches` and the\0asystem test against the real roster are what catch a mismatch here.\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0aRosterNode\00\00\00\00\00\09\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\06active\00\00\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\07address\00\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\09joined_at\00\00\00\00\00\00\04\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0elast_heartbeat\00\00\00\00\00\04\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\04name\00\00\00\10\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\06staked\00\00\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0ftunnel_endpoint\00\00\00\00\10\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0cunbonding_at\00\00\03\e8\00\00\00\04\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\09volunteer\00\00\00\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\01\00\00\01\10Emitted on a spend-mode ownership transfer. Endpoints are opaque commitments;\0aan observer can see the token changed hands but not who to. Successive\0aspends of one token are linkable to each other; that per-token linkage\0ais accepted (see `docs/architecture/spend-mode.md`).\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0aSpendEvent\00\00\00\00\00\04\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0dephemeral_key\00\00\00\00\00\03\ee\00\00\00 \00\00\00\00\00\00\00\14new_owner_commitment\00\00\03\ee\00\00\00 \00\00\008Which record moved. The key alone does not identify one.\00\00\00\07slot_id\00\00\00\00\04\00\00\00\8eThe nonce **after** this spend. An observer rebuilding owner\0ahistory from events needs it to know where the next\0aauthorisation has to be made.\00\00\00\00\00\0bspend_nonce\00\00\00\00\04\00\00\00\03\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0aTokenState\00\00\00\00\00\04\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\08Printing\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\06Active\00\00\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\08Redeemed\00\00\00\02\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\09Cancelled\00\00\00\00\00\00\03\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0bTokenRecord\00\00\00\00\0f\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\06amount\00\00\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\e2SHA-256 of the canonical Path-B `chain_data` blob, committed by the\0adepositor at registration. Binds redemption to the real signed chain so\0aa chain cannot be forged from public data (see\0a`docs/architecture/security-model.md`).\00\00\00\00\00\0achain_hash\00\00\00\00\03\ee\00\00\00 \00\00\02\95Public half of the note's **claim key**, fixed at registration.\0a\0aThe secret half travels inside the note container and is never sent\0ato this contract. Path B redemption presents a signature from it\0arather than the chain preimage alone, which is what stops a\0aredemption being lifted out of the ledger: `chain_data` is published\0aby any attempt, successful or failed, and a failed one leaves the\0anote Active with its secret in public view.\0a\0aThis does not make the note non-bearer. The key is in the file, not\0atied to a person: copy the file and you copy the right to redeem.\0aSpend mode is the opposite trade and is already recipient-bound, so\0ait does not need one.\00\00\00\00\00\00\0cclaim_pubkey\00\00\03\ee\00\00\00 \00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0acreated_at\00\00\00\00\00\04\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0dephemeral_key\00\00\00\00\00\03\ee\00\00\00 \00\00\00\00\00\00\00\08event_id\00\00\03\ee\00\00\00 \00\00\002Spend mode for this token (fixed at registration).\00\00\00\00\00\04mode\00\00\07\d0\00\00\00\09TokenMode\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\08node_fee\00\00\00\04\00\00\00\9aThe current owner commitment `SHA-256(\22kntr_v1:spend:owner\22 || owner_pubkey)`.\0aOverwritten each `spend`. Unused (and unchecked) when `mode == PureBearer`.\00\00\00\00\00\10owner_commitment\00\00\03\ee\00\00\00 \00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0cparticipants\00\00\03\ea\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0bredeemed_at\00\00\00\00\04\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\07slot_id\00\00\00\00\04\00\00\01\e7How many times this note has been spent on. Part of both owner\0adigests, so a signature is good for exactly one transfer.\0a\0aWithout it the digest would be `(ek, current_commitment,\0anew_commitment)`, which repeats whenever a note returns to an\0aowner commitment it held before \e2\80\94 and the static pay tag (owner\0aindex 0) is a reusable address, so a note coming back as change\0aor a refund does exactly that. The earlier signature would then\0areplay, and a former payee could take the note back.\00\00\00\00\0bspend_nonce\00\00\00\00\04\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\05state\00\00\00\00\00\07\d0\00\00\00\0aTokenState\00\00\00\00\00TCopied from the slot: which `participants` volunteer. See\0a[`PrintSlot::volunteers`].\00\00\00\0avolunteers\00\00\00\00\00\04\00\00\00\01\00\00\00OPositions abandoned after a draw, burned out of the escrow at cancel or\0aexpiry.\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0cForfeitEvent\00\00\00\03\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\06amount\00\00\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\09positions\00\00\00\00\00\00\04\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\07slot_id\00\00\00\00\04\00\00\00\01\00\00\02\87A volunteer's fee, destroyed instead of credited.\0a\0aOne per volunteer per settlement, redemption included, so anyone can\0acheck from events alone that a volunteer was never paid for the\0asettlements it volunteered on.\0a\0aTerms are per address and fixed when a print is requested. An\0aaddress that volunteered from its first join is never credited, so\0aits `Accrued` balance stays at zero. One that converted keeps what it\0aaccrued while paid, and is still credited by prints requested before\0ait converted.\0a\0aIf the pay token refused the burn, the settlement also emits a\0a[`FeeLockedEvent`]: the amount stayed in the mint instead, where\0anothing can move it.\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0eFeeBurnedEvent\00\00\00\00\00\03\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\06amount\00\00\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\04node\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\07slot_id\00\00\00\00\04\00\00\00\01\00\00\01[The pay token refused a settlement's burn, so the volunteers' fees\0a(`amount`, the settlement's total) stay in the mint's balance. No\0aentry point can move them: they are no node's `Accrued` and no slot's\0aescrow, so they are as unreachable as burned. A burn that traps\0awould instead have locked the holder's payout or the depositor's\0arefund forever.\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0eFeeLockedEvent\00\00\00\00\00\02\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\06amount\00\00\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\07slot_id\00\00\00\00\04\00\00\00\01\00\00\001An address's registered pair (`DataKey::PairOf`).\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0eRegisteredPair\00\00\00\00\00\02\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\07partner\00\00\00\00\13\00\00\00YThe ledger the pair was registered in. A pair may claim only on\0aslots requested after it.\00\00\00\00\00\00\0dregistered_at\00\00\00\00\00\00\04\00\00\00\01\00\00\01\85Emitted once per confirmer credited by an abandoned print.\0a\0aRedemption reports its payouts in aggregate on the `Redeem*` events.\0aWithout this, settling a cancelled or expired slot would publish\0anothing, and a node that had earned a fee could learn of it only by\0apolling `get_accrued` against every slot it ever touched. The amount is what this settlement credited, not the running\0abalance.\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0fFeeAccruedEvent\00\00\00\00\03\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\06amount\00\00\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\04node\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\07slot_id\00\00\00\00\04\00\00\00\01\00\00\01`How nodes select themselves into a print\0a(`docs/architecture/node-selection.md`).\0a\0aImmutable, like the rest of the config. The beacon fields name a drand\0achain of scheme `bls-unchained-g1-rfc9380` (quicknet). The scheme\0aitself -- hash-to-curve DST, signature group, message -- is fixed in\0athe contract, so only the chain's own constants are parameters.\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0fSelectionConfig\00\00\00\00\08\00\00\00\22Unix time of the beacon's round 1.\00\00\00\00\00\0ebeacon_genesis\00\00\00\00\00\06\00\00\00\c0Rounds between a request and the round that seeds it. The round\0a`round_at(request time) + beacon_lead` must not exist yet when the\0arequest lands, or a depositor could know the draw in advance.\00\00\00\0bbeacon_lead\00\00\00\00\06\00\00\00\17Seconds between rounds.\00\00\00\00\0dbeacon_period\00\00\00\00\00\00\06\00\00\00>The beacon's group key: G2, uncompressed (Soroban's encoding).\00\00\00\00\00\09beacon_pk\00\00\00\00\00\03\ee\00\00\00\c0\00\00\00VLedgers after `seed_print` during which a lower score may still\0adisplace a higher one.\00\00\00\00\00\0cclaim_window\00\00\00\04\00\00\00\87Seconds after round `R` is due before `seed_fallback` may seed a\0aslot nobody has seeded from the beacon. At least\0a`MIN_FALLBACK_DELAY`.\00\00\00\00\0efallback_delay\00\00\00\00\00\06\00\00\00VLedgers a node must have been on the roster before it may claim\0a0 turns the check off.\00\00\00\00\00\0cmin_node_age\00\00\00\04\00\00\00QLedgers a selected pair has to confirm its link before the\0adepositor may skip it.\00\00\00\00\00\00\0dserve_timeout\00\00\00\00\00\00\04\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\10FeesClaimedEvent\00\00\00\02\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\06amount\00\00\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\04node\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\01\00\00\00;The slot is seeded: pairs may claim until `claim_deadline`.\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\10PrintSeededEvent\00\00\00\05\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0cbeacon_round\00\00\00\06\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0eclaim_deadline\00\00\00\00\00\04\00\00\00!Interior positions to fill (`k`).\00\00\00\00\00\00\09positions\00\00\00\00\00\00\04\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\04seed\00\00\03\ee\00\00\00 \00\00\00\00\00\00\00\07slot_id\00\00\00\00\04\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\10RedeemByKeyEvent\00\00\00\07\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\06amount\00\00\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0dephemeral_key\00\00\00\00\00\03\ee\00\00\00 \00\00\01\0bWho submitted the transaction.\0a\0a**Not who was paid.** `redeem_*` takes a separate `recipient`, so\0aan indexer reading this as the payee is wrong every time the two\0adiffer -- which is the ordinary case for a redemption directed\0aanywhere but the submitter's own account.\00\00\00\00\06holder\00\00\00\00\00\13\00\00\00lTotal node fees credited to participants' accrual balances (claimable\0avia `claim_fees`), not paid instantly.\00\00\00\11node_fees_accrued\00\00\00\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00XVolunteers' fees, burned. `amount + node_fees_accrued +\0anode_fees_burned` is the escrow.\00\00\00\10node_fees_burned\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00$Who the escrow was actually paid to.\00\00\00\09recipient\00\00\00\00\00\00\13\00\00\01\0fWhich record was redeemed.\0a\0aThe key does not identify one: records are keyed by slot, so two\0amay legitimately name the same `ephemeral_key`. `TokenActive` and\0a`Spend` carry it too; the redemption events need it most, since\0athey are the ones that say where the money went.\00\00\00\00\07slot_id\00\00\00\00\04\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\10SlotExpiredEvent\00\00\00\07\00\00\00\1cAs on `PrintCancelledEvent`.\00\00\00\06burned\00\00\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\09depositor\00\00\00\00\00\00\13\00\00\00=As on `PrintCancelledEvent`: the settled part of the deposit.\00\00\00\00\00\00\06earned\00\00\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\08event_id\00\00\03\ee\00\00\00 \00\00\00\1cAs on `PrintCancelledEvent`.\00\00\00\09forfeited\00\00\00\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\06refund\00\00\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\07slot_id\00\00\00\00\04\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\10TokenActiveEvent\00\00\00\08\00\00\00oThe **gross** escrow. Node fees come off it at redemption, so\0athis is not the figure a `Redeem*` event reports.\00\00\00\00\06amount\00\00\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\ecThe chain commitment, and the claim key.\0a\0aWithout these an indexer following events alone cannot tell\0awhich note a given `ephemeral_key` belongs to \e2\80\94 and since\0arecords are keyed by slot, two of them may legitimately name\0athe same key.\00\00\00\0achain_hash\00\00\00\00\03\ee\00\00\00 \00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0cclaim_pubkey\00\00\03\ee\00\00\00 \00\00\00\12Who registered it.\00\00\00\00\00\09depositor\00\00\00\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0dephemeral_key\00\00\00\00\00\03\ee\00\00\00 \00\00\00\00\00\00\00\08event_id\00\00\03\ee\00\00\00 \00\00\00\22Spend mode, fixed at registration.\00\00\00\00\00\04mode\00\00\07\d0\00\00\00\09TokenMode\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\07slot_id\00\00\00\00\04\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\11PrintRequestEvent\00\00\00\00\00\00\08\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\06amount\00\00\00\00\00\0b\00\00\004The beacon round whose signature will seed the slot.\00\00\00\0cbeacon_round\00\00\00\06\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\09depositor\00\00\00\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\08event_id\00\00\03\ee\00\00\00 \00\00\00BThe depositor's own end pairs. The interior is chosen by the draw.\00\00\00\00\00\0afirst_pair\00\00\00\00\07\d0\00\00\00\09PairEntry\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\09last_pair\00\00\00\00\00\07\d0\00\00\00\09PairEntry\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\07slot_id\00\00\00\00\04\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0btotal_pairs\00\00\00\00\04\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\12LinkConfirmedEvent\00\00\00\00\00\05\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0fcompleted_links\00\00\00\00\04\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\09confirmer\00\00\00\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0alink_index\00\00\00\00\00\04\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\12partial_public_key\00\00\00\00\03\ee\00\00\00 \00\00\00\00\00\00\00\07slot_id\00\00\00\00\04\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\84The slot was seeded by `seed_fallback` rather than the beacon. Published\0abeside the ordinary `seeded` event, which carries the seed.\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\12PrintFallbackEvent\00\00\00\00\00\02\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0cbeacon_round\00\00\00\06\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\07slot_id\00\00\00\00\04\00\00\00\01\00\00\00;Selection closed: `pairs` is the chain, end pairs included.\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\12PrintSelectedEvent\00\00\00\00\00\02\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\05pairs\00\00\00\00\00\03\ea\00\00\07\d0\00\00\00\09PairEntry\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\07slot_id\00\00\00\00\04\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\12RedeemByChainEvent\00\00\00\00\00\07\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\06amount\00\00\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0dephemeral_key\00\00\00\00\00\03\ee\00\00\00 \00\00\00XWho submitted the transaction. **Not who was paid** -- see\0a[`RedeemByKeyEvent::holder`].\00\00\00\06holder\00\00\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\a1Total node fees credited to participants' accrual balances, claimable\0avia `claim_fees`. Safe on Path B because the chain hash binds\0aredemption to the real chain.\00\00\00\00\00\00\11node_fees_accrued\00\00\00\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00GVolunteers' fees, burned -- see [`RedeemByKeyEvent::node_fees_burned`].\00\00\00\00\10node_fees_burned\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00$Who the escrow was actually paid to.\00\00\00\09recipient\00\00\00\00\00\00\13\00\00\00@Which record was redeemed \e2\80\94 see [`RedeemByKeyEvent::slot_id`].\00\00\00\07slot_id\00\00\00\00\04\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\13PrintCancelledEvent\00\00\00\00\06\00\00\007Volunteer confirmers' fees, destroyed rather than paid.\00\00\00\00\06burned\00\00\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\97What the confirmers were paid out of the deposit. `refund +\0aearned + burned` is the whole of it, which is the check a\0adepositor following events needs.\00\00\00\00\06earned\00\00\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\